**Verdict on the claim: refuted.** Cycles 133 through 140 produced one more structural file that has never executed, a 185-action plan for the next one, three donor VIs, and the discovery that every ring slot write built since cycle 131 uses the wrong primitive. Nothing the user can run today is different from what they could run at the 08:13 review. This is the fifth consecutive refutation.

Limits of this review: `claudeDev\` is outside the repository, so file states are as the logs record them. Costs come from `tools/bench/cycle_runner.log`. No external claims were needed, so no URLs are cited. Two counter faults in the attached brief: the cadence line says 5 retrospectives since the last review, but 8 cycles ran (133 to 140); cycles 135, 138 and 139 have no retrospective file in `archive/peer/`, so the review cadence undercounts spend by three cycles. And `Track_v6_CPU_core_v0.vi` / `Track_v6_CPU_queue_v0.vi` are still listed as deliverables while no file of that name exists under `2. Tracking`; only recipe scripts name them (`tools/recipes/build_track_v6_core.py:48`). Fifth review to report the same phantom. Also, this review carries the same id as the morning one, so its archive file will collide with `archive/peer/2026-10-02-outcome-review-20261002.md`.

